272 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (The HAND2HANDAPP is a mobile-firstplatform designed to connect customers with local daily-wage workers and service providers. Many unskilled workers have limited digital visibility, making it difficult to find consistent employment, while customers often struggle to identify reliable workers for basic services. To address this gap, the platform enables direct, location-based connections between workers and customers through a simple and accessible interface.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
273 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (This project designs  the system using the MERN stack \(MongoDB, Express.js, React.js, and Node.js\) with a role- based architecture. Customers can search and hire workers, while workers can manage their profiles, list services, and showcase their experience. By focusing on a secure and scalable backend, simplified onboarding, and transparent interaction flows, the platform aims to improve worker visibility, build customer trust, and create a more inclusive digital ecosystem for daily-wage employment.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
